  "final_decision": "RETAIN_F3",
  "decision_rationale": "None of the 4 tested hypotheses (variance stretch, isotonic calibration, linear recalibration, squared_error loss) improved the within-25% metric on grouped CV. The F3 baseline (69.54% CV) remains the best validated model. The range-compression failure mode is inherent to the absolute_error loss, but fixing it (squared_error) trades range coverage for tolerance accuracy without net gain. The dominant limitation is the data: district-level aggregate yields with static climate normals cannot support higher accuracy."
